Through the Stair
For my non-linear narrative project, I am going to be creating a Twine story that takes place on a staircase in a building. The entire story will not be told from one person’s perspective, but instead, different memories from different people can be seen through different moments that the player can click on, such as “Morning Rush,” “Late Night,” or “Roof” to name a few. Even though the player can click on whatever they want in terms of different moments, the story can still be pieced together for the reader, as the staircase links all the stories together throughout the building. There is no clear beginning or end, giving the player constant options in terms of how they wish to piece together the story.
I chose to do this prompt because I really like architecture, and I think spaces can be filled with memories and how the space is made can affect how people interact with each other in that particular space. I did not go with a choose your own adventure because I wanted the focus to be more on atmosphere, and how you move through a space and how that space can connect people throughout the space. The staircase is the scene and narrator for this story of how ordinary interactions can create a sense of community within a shared space.
